# The channel is sticky and changes only with a new version: the
# sounding note's off goes to the channel it was started on. The
# state's channel is the playing version's (1 until the swap at beat
# 2, then 5); a track with only a waiting version shows the channel
# it will start on (track 2, 9).
open virtual
track 1 60:2
  takes over at beat 0.000 (t0)
play continue
  was playing: 0
runto 1
track 1:5 62:2
  takes over at beat 2.000 (t5040)
state
  seq: PLAYING beat 1.000 (t2520) tempo 120 tracks 1
  track 1: notes 1 ch 1 mute 0 loop 1 vel 100 length 2.000 (t5040) pending 1 position 1.000 (t2520)
runto 5
log
  0.000 t0 0.000ms ON  ch1 60 v100
  2.000 t5040 1000.000ms OFF ch1 60
  2.000 t5040 1000.000ms ON  ch5 62 v100
  4.000 t10080 2000.000ms OFF ch5 62
  4.000 t10080 2000.000ms ON  ch5 62 v100
track 2:9 50:1
  takes over at beat 5.000 (t12600)
state
  seq: PLAYING beat 5.000 (t12600) tempo 120 tracks 2
  track 1: notes 1 ch 5 mute 0 loop 1 vel 100 length 2.000 (t5040) pending 0 position 1.000 (t2520)
  track 2: notes 0 ch 9 mute 0 loop 1 vel 100 length 0.000 (t0) pending 1 position 0.000 (t0)
track 1 64:2
  takes over at beat 6.000 (t15120)
runto 7
log
  5.000 t12600 2500.000ms ON  ch9 50 v100
  6.000 t15120 3000.000ms OFF ch5 62
  6.000 t15120 3000.000ms OFF ch9 50
  6.000 t15120 3000.000ms ON  ch5 64 v100
  6.000 t15120 3000.000ms ON  ch9 50 v100
